          "filename": "1931- The cornerstone laid for the Botanic Garden. (22346900644).jpg",
          "caption": "After years of debate, it was decided to move the Botanic Garden to its present site on Maryland Avenue. At the cornerstone laying, Senator Simeon C. Fess, Chairman of the Joint Committee on the Library, holds the trowel. The other gentlemen present are, from left to right: Horace D. Rouzer, Assistant Architect of the Capitol; George W. Hess, Director of the Botanic Garden; Eugene Pugh of the George A. Fuller Co.; and David Lynn, Architect of the Capitol.",
